----------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT CAUSE OF THE RED GATE — PRE-EXISTING, OUT-OF-SCOPE CONTAMINATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Every one of the 226 iOS / 8+ macOS compile errors is in OTHER, committed,
unmodified surfaces (verified `git status` clean; verified 0 references to any
AlertStudio* symbol). They are duplicate type / facade declarations produced by
sibling P4 prompts, e.g.:
  * dashboard-widgets: 'SafetyModel' defined twice (SafetyFeaturesWidget.Model.swift
    + SafetyHistoryWidget.Model.swift); 'ChargeStateDTO' / 'ChargeSessionDTO' /
    'ChargeUnitPrefs' / 'ChargeStatusProjection' defined twice (ChargeStatusWidget*
    + ChargeStatusLiveWidget*); 'FleetStatsBarModel' defined in both
    feature-views/FleetStatsBar.Model.swift and dashboard-widgets/FleetStatsBarWidget.Model.swift.
  * feature-views: 'MonthlyCostStrings' defined twice (MonthlyCostTable.Model.swift
    + MonthlyCostChart.Model.swift) -> "ambiguous use of 'string'".
  Sample:
    ChargeStatusLiveWidget.Adapter.swift:173: 'ChargeStateDTO' is ambiguous for type lookup
    ChargeSessionChartWidget.Model.swift:74:  'ChargeSessionDTO' is ambiguous for type lookup
The macOS step additionally requires a development signing certificate that is not
available on this runner (an environment-capability gap, independent of source).
The single swiftlint violation is likewise in a pre-existing dashboard-widget file.

Per the engineering rule "Don't fix pre-existing issues unrelated to your task"
and the prompt's own "Out of Scope: Other surfaces in the same feature (each has
its own prompt)", these sibling-surface defects were NOT modified. Touching them
would corrupt other prompts' intended outputs.

